{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And there went up with him both chariots and horsemen.</b> In order to guard the way and so that they would not detain them from the burial, Esau and his sons did so, for Joseph knew the malice of their hearts, as is found written in the book of Yosef ben Gurion: for Zepho son of Eliphaz son of Esau lay in wait for them on the road and quarreled with them over this, until they waged battle, and the hand of Joseph prevailed and they seized him together with the choicest of his warriors and brought him to Egypt, and he remained there all his days in prison until Joseph died; and when Joseph died he fled from there and went to the land of Kittim and ruled over Kittim in Rome, and in the end he ruled over the land of Greece, Italy — and he was the first king in Rome, and he built the first temple in Rome. Therefore Scripture says ״גם רכב גם פרשים״ — 'both chariots and horsemen' — for besides the chariots and horsemen that went up with him by way of honor, men of war went up with him, such as patrols and guards, to do battle against them if they needed to, and this is the reason for the גם — the instances of 'also' — that come to include." "<b>And the camp was very heavy [great].</b> It is possible to say that it also alludes to the camp of the supernal beings who came to guard him now in his death just as they came to him to guard him in his lifetime; and perhaps this camp is those angels of Elohim whom he encountered, whom he called (Genesis 32) מחנה אלהים — 'the camp of Elohim' — and from this it says כבד מאד, 'very great'; and in the two words there is an allusion to the special Name in its numerical value and its letter-fill."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {0 "The text reads עשו ובניו 'Esau and his sons'; context and the subsequent narrative about Zepho son of Eliphaz (Esau's grandson) suggest this is the intended referent. תיירים rendered hyper-literally as 'patrols' (from תור, to scout/patrol)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:01.564646643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}